# GludioSwordGuardUseSkill (35060, a sword guard mercenary) sees the character, who neither
# defends nor owns its castle: on a draw of 0 of 10000 it shouts NpcString 1800012, and it
# wants to attack the character with weight 200 (a desire, not rendered). Its own
# see-creature hook replaces GludioHold's, so no life-time gate holds it back. Its other
# hooks only queue desires and hate, which the format cannot check (#3983):
# tests/ai/siege_guard_sword_test.go covers them.
character Hunter 20
random always 0
script script.ai.individual.DefaultNpc
script script.ai.siegeguards.GludioHold.GludioHold
script script.ai.siegeguards.GludioHold.GludioSwordGuard
script script.ai.siegeguards.GludioHold.GludioSwordGuardUseSkill
npc guard 35060 SiegeGuard 600 0 0

approach guard
  S NpcSay obj=guard type=1 npc=1035060 text="Death to those who challenge the Lords of Dawn!"
